cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use NeuroCorridor-3D in teaching, workshops, or academic research, please cite it using the metadata in this file."
type: software
title: "NeuroCorridor-3D: Zero-Build Interactive 3D Stereotactic Neuroanatomy, Fiber Tractography & Surgical Corridor Planning Sandbox"
version: "1.0.0"
date-released: "2026-11-20"
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/neurocorridor-3d/neurocorridor-3d"
url: "https://neurocorridor-3d.github.io/neurocorridor-3d/"
authors:
  - name: "NeuroCorridor-3D Contributors"
abstract: >-
  NeuroCorridor-3D is a zero-build, 100% browser-local static web application
  for interactive 3D stereotactic neuroanatomy education and research in
  MNI-152 RAS+ millimeter coordinates. It integrates 8 eloquent cortical,
  deep-gray, cranial-nerve, and neurovascular regions (11 lateralized
  structures), 6 white-matter fiber tract systems (10 Catmull-Rom spline
  bundles with Anatomical and DTI DEC RGB visualization), 5 curated
  neurosurgical teaching cases, analytical real-time corridor clearance
  computation, deterministic trajectory optimization, synchronized radiological
  tri-planar slices, a down-the-barrel Probe's-Eye view, client-side MNI-152
  NIfTI-1 (.nii/.nii.gz) lesion mask overlay with zero uploads, and a
  10-question interactive neuroanatomy quiz. Educational and research sandbox
  only; not approved for clinical neuronavigation.
keywords:
  - neurosurgery
  - neuroanatomy
  - stereotaxy
  - MNI-152
  - fiber-tractography
  - surgical-corridor-planning
  - nifti
  - medical-education
  - open-science
  - browser-local
